{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes","id":1401821,"title":"Random thought on Threshold Successes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-08T18:55:35-07:00","id":1401821,"title":"Random thought on Threshold Successes","content":"So I was reading a post on Craft (I know, I know) and crazy-high threshold success, and had a random thought. Threshold successes have always been kinda a funny thing in Exalted. In many circumstances, they don't even matter, because once you hit the difficulty, there isn't a logical way of &quot;winning harder&quot;. But in the places it <i>does</i> do something (accuracy in combat, Craft, Sorcerous Workings), it can be problematic for balance.<br /> <br /> So, I was thinking. What if, after penalties etc, but <i>before</i> calculating Threshold successes, you applied a scaling factor. The first 5 would be as normal, but then the next 5 threshold successes would cost 2 extra successes each, then the next 5 would cost 3 each, the 4 each, etc. Assuming normal Exalts-roll-up mechanics, on a single roll, the result would be:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 150px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"> Extra<br /> Successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Threshold<br /> Successes</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">8</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">15</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">10</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">20</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">12</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">30</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">15</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">40</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">18</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">50</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">20</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">75</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">25</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">100</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">30</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">200</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">43</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So rounding cutoffs aside, more successes <i>is</i> still better, but within the context of a single roll they are vastly tempered. Plus, it's pretty easy to apply if you're counting physical dice.<br /> <br /> Full disclosure, this idea partly came from the excellent VP mechanics in the board game Lords of Vegas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T20:36:04-07:00","id":1401841,"title":"","content":"The dice tricks in the Craft charms lead to complicated bookkeeping and too many extra successes, and this seems like it would help with the too many extra successes problem at the cost of making the complicated bookkeeping worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T21:35:36-07:00","id":1401852,"title":"","content":"I remember hearing this kind of thing being talked about in one of the Exalted Essence interviews, where I think Monica noted that there were a lot of times where the corebook of Exalted says &quot;Five successes is a lot, like, the peak of difficulty&quot;<br /> <br /> And then basically never say what seven, nine, or <i>fifteen</i> successes means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T00:12:33-07:00","id":1401870,"title":"","content":"The difficulty section is kind of a riot when you think about it too hard. Doing an appendectomy in the dark in a storm with a basic knife is like Diff 3. A bank vault is only DC 2 to pick, and a first age sorcery lock is 4. <br /> <br /> I had a player roll 11 successes on a swords dance and he almost entirely changed the performative culture of Fajad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T07:41:29-07:00","id":1401916,"title":"","content":"The Difficulty Chart is pretty much exactly right, if you assume that only heroes Stunt and a basic success with no threshold successes means you only just succeed.<br /> <br /> The Exalted are just that good.<br /> <br /> As for this idea... it's neat but I'm not going to add another step to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-09-2020, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T08:30:06-07:00","id":1401918,"title":"","content":"I've come to see the &quot;15 successes&quot; thing as mostly a kind of meaningless fluke of the Exalted system and what it's trying to do. If you're an exalt who's super focused in an area, and you spend over a dozen motes activating a slew of charms, then basically you do the thing. It's just that the way the dicepool-success system works you're always going to have a fluke of a super low roll or a super high one.<br /> <br /> So if you want to really lower the chances of failure, you need to pile on more and more dice, which pushes the curve up. You don't really care to roll 10 successes, you care that your chances of rolling less than 5 are now below 1%. The game could, and sometimes does, represent this with flat autosuccesses, but after a certain point that completely negates any chance of failure, and that's less exciting, even if it's basically the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T10:18:07-07:00","id":1401935,"title":"","content":"This doesn't look...profitable, so to say.<br /> It's significantly extra work (you WILL look at an extra chart every other roll) for what gain?<br /> <br /> In damage, if you are hitting those ludicrous thresholds capping them like this won't significantly change the pace of the fight.<br /> In craft, those that hit such silly numbers are generally past caring for the gains as well.<br /> Workings don't benefit from exploding all that much in the first place, in most cases you'll just be cutting the Working time to 1-2 weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T10:45:39-07:00","id":1401937,"title":"","content":"I agree with Synapse. Like is there going to be a meaningful difference between 10 vs 15 threshold successes?<br /> <br /> I just make a &quot;critical&quot; success at anything that's 3 or more successes beyond the listed difficulty. Is it easy for exalts to achieve? Yea, but it's still a big difference between those who dabble and those who specialize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T11:44:28-07:00","id":1401940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401852#post1401852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember hearing this kind of thing being talked about in one of the Exalted Essence interviews, where I think Monica noted that there were a lot of times where the corebook of Exalted says &quot;Five successes is a lot, like, the peak of difficulty&quot;<br /> <br /> And then basically never say what seven, nine, or <i>fifteen</i> successes means.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally appreciate that Ex3 doesn't say that should get extra for threshold successes in general like 2nd edition did with Legendary Successes because more than once I've seen characters ridiculously over-succeeded on social rolls and getting arguably negative consequences because the Storyteller wanted the outcome to be portrayed as &quot;legendary&quot; more than they wanted it to be &quot;successful&quot;.<br /> <br /> It was actually Monica herself who introduced me to the concept of &quot;failing forwards&quot; which helped me see that a lot of tables were treating a 20+ success social roll like how I might treat a botched one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T12:40:51-07:00","id":1401946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401940#post1401940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally appreciate that Ex3 doesn't say that should get extra for threshold successes in general like 2nd edition did with Legendary Successes because more than once I've seen characters ridiculously over-succeeded on social rolls and getting arguably negative consequences because the Storyteller wanted the outcome to be portrayed as &quot;legendary&quot; more than they wanted it to be &quot;successful&quot;.<br /> <br /> It was actually Monica herself who introduced me to the concept of &quot;failing forwards&quot; which helped me see that a lot of tables were treating a 20+ success social roll like how I might treat a botched one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean like, you convinced the sultan to reject the Realm's offer of becoming a satrapy <i>so hard</i> that now he's mobilizing his army and conscripting civilians to march on the Realm in open war, which is really not something you wanted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T13:10:54-07:00","id":1401954,"title":"","content":"There's definitely room for some good &quot;Gone Horribly Right&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T13:48:12-07:00","id":1401957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401870#post1401870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difficulty section is kind of a riot when you think about it too hard. Doing an appendectomy in the dark in a storm with a basic knife is like Diff 3. A bank vault is only DC 2 to pick, and a first age sorcery lock is 4.<br /> <br /> I had a player roll 11 successes on a swords dance and he almost entirely changed the performative culture of Fajad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the example DCs have nothing to do with what rolls look like once Charms come into play. The examples for DC 5 are the kind of things I'd point to as feats of Solar excellence, rather than the sorts of things you can do reliably with secondary (or even tertiary) skills.<br /> <br /> (Not to say that you should need fifty Athletics Charms to run for 72 hours straight, but you shouldn't be able to do it without <i>some </i>kind of investment in Dex+Athletics beyond a few dots and an Excellency)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 07-09-2020, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T14:13:52-07:00","id":1401965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401916#post1401916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Difficulty Chart is pretty much exactly right, if you assume that only heroes Stunt and a basic success with no threshold successes means you only just succeed.<br /> <br /> The Exalted are just that good.<br /> <br /> As for this idea... it's neat but I'm not going to add another step to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what happens when you compare it to the dice pools for mortals? Are non-Exalted characters supposed to get different difficulties?<br /> <br /> A priest with martial training can remove an appendix in the dead of night, without sufficient light, in the midst of a howling storm 73% of the time. A professional spy can pick a lock in the same conditions 87% of the time.<br /> <br /> If plucking a gem from a nest of writhing serpents without being bitten is an example of pickpocketing, our spy can expect a 69% success rate. At least in this case, the consequences of failure are dire, so the roll might not be attempted even if the chances of success are well better than 50-50.<br /> <br /> Reading a letter in pitch blackness is something elite troops can do 48% of the time. Failing doesn't represent danger here, so if you're trapped in the dark with a couple of your bodyguards and need to read a letter you can just pass it from one to the other and probably one will be able to read it.<br /> <br /> Horse archers have the same tracking dice pool, so if you imagine a similarly impressive feat of tracking (maybe tracking a flying foe using Stormwind Rider by the way the wind pushes the leaves on the ground out of formation), a horse archer has a 48% shot to achieve it. Note that horse archers are specifically called out as not necessarily specially trained elites but just people who learned those skills from how it fits into their lifestyle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T15:56:42-07:00","id":1401982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401957#post1401957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the example DCs have nothing to do with what rolls look like once Charms come into play. The examples for DC 5 are the kind of things I'd point to as feats of Solar excellence, rather than the sorts of things you can do reliably with secondary (or even tertiary) skills.<br /> <br /> (Not to say that you should need fifty Athletics Charms to run for 72 hours straight, but you shouldn't be able to do it without <i>some </i>kind of investment in Dex+Athletics beyond a few dots and an Excellency)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue is exacerbated by how Attributes and Abilities don't scale in an intuitive way. Like, there's no &quot;beginner&quot; skill level, the moment you have a dot in something you know what you're doing.<br /> <br /> 1-you know what you're doing<br /> 2-you know what you're doing+<br /> 3-you're a genius<br /> 4-you're a genius+<br /> 5-you're a genius++<br /> <br /> So someone with a <i>mere</i> Dex 2 Athletics 3 is already quite limber and an athletic talent. If you add magic that doubles their potential, I wouldn't put it past them to accomplish a mythical feat like running 72 hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T16:09:12-07:00","id":1401984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401965#post1401965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But what happens when you compare it to the dice pools for mortals? Are non-Exalted characters supposed to get different difficulties?<br /> <br /> A priest with martial training can remove an appendix in the dead of night, without sufficient light, in the midst of a howling storm 73% of the time. A professional spy can pick a lock in the same conditions 87% of the time.<br /> <br /> If plucking a gem from a nest of writhing serpents without being bitten is an example of pickpocketing, our spy can expect a 69% success rate. At least in this case, the consequences of failure are dire, so the roll might not be attempted even if the chances of success are well better than 50-50.<br /> <br /> Reading a letter in pitch blackness is something elite troops can do 48% of the time. Failing doesn't represent danger here, so if you're trapped in the dark with a couple of your bodyguards and need to read a letter you can just pass it from one to the other and probably one will be able to read it.<br /> <br /> Horse archers have the same tracking dice pool, so if you imagine a similarly impressive feat of tracking (maybe tracking a flying foe using Stormwind Rider by the way the wind pushes the leaves on the ground out of formation), a horse archer has a 48% shot to achieve it. Note that horse archers are specifically called out as not necessarily specially trained elites but just people who learned those skills from how it fits into their lifestyle.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;As great heroes, Exalted characters are assumed to possess abundant confdence and competence. Tasks which run-of-the-mill individuals in Creation would consider challenging (such as picking a lock or removing a patient\u2019s appendix without killing him) are ordinary fare for heroes. Such tasks are appropriate for difficulty 1.&quot;<br /> <br /> Heroic characters use the heroic difficulty chart. Run-of-the-mill characters don't.<br /> <br /> A heroic priest can perform surgery at night in a storm 73% of the time. Your average priest cannot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-10-2020, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T17:16:27-07:00","id":1401992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401852#post1401852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember hearing this kind of thing being talked about in one of the Exalted Essence interviews, where I think Monica noted that there were a lot of times where the corebook of Exalted says &quot;Five successes is a lot, like, the peak of difficulty&quot;<br /> <br /> And then basically never say what seven, nine, or <i>fifteen</i> successes means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting.<br /> <br /> With third edition rules as-written the difficulty for the actual action plateaus at 5. However while attempting surgery might be difficulty 3 (Intelligence + Medicine) roll, attempting it in pitch darkness might impose a -3 dice penalty to your roll if the Storyteller wanted to acknowledge the adverse circumstances. <br /> <br /> For a simpler system it would make more sense to remove that penalty and increase the difficulty of the surgery roll directly rather than mess around with a dice penalty that people seem to forget exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T20:39:34-07:00","id":1402011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401992#post1401992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting.<br /> <br /> With third edition rules as-written the difficulty for the actual action plateaus at 5. However while attempting surgery might be difficulty 3 (Intelligence + Medicine) roll, attempting it in pitch darkness might impose a -3 dice penalty to your roll if the Storyteller wanted to acknowledge the adverse circumstances.<br /> <br /> For a simpler system it would make more sense to remove that penalty and increase the difficulty of the surgery roll directly rather than mess around with a dice penalty that people seem to forget exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Essence is gonna shake the difficulty chart out slightly.<br /> <br /> Like... &quot;Difficulties for things that Exalts should bother rolling for should START at 3. Beating up a group of drunks when you're a goddamn Exalt would be Difficulty 3 and easier tasks, don't bother rolling&quot; and I think I recall hearing the game may have charts for what 7 successes or more would mean for Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T22:08:00-07:00","id":1402013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402011#post1402011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Essence is gonna shake the difficulty chart out slightly.<br /> <br /> Like... &amp;quot;Difficulties for things that Exalts should bother rolling for should START at 3. Beating up a group of drunks when you're a goddamn Exalt would be Difficulty 3 and easier tasks, don't bother rolling&amp;quot; and I think I recall hearing the game may have charts for what 7 successes or more would mean for Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, ExEss is going to set the difficulty chart at 3-7, instead of one to five, and I think that Monica wants to include guidance on dealing with 10+ successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T23:55:35-07:00","id":1402019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401946#post1401946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean like, you convinced the sultan to reject the Realm's offer of becoming a satrapy <i>so hard</i> that now he's mobilizing his army and conscripting civilians to march on the Realm in open war, which is really not something you wanted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, precisely that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401954#post1401954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's definitely room for some good &quot;Gone Horribly Right&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if I see an obvious problem with what they're suggesting not as a monkeys paw outcome based primarily on the number of successes rolled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T03:49:03-07:00","id":1402037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401992#post1401992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With third edition rules as-written the difficulty for the actual action plateaus at 5. However while attempting surgery might be difficulty 3 (Intelligence + Medicine) roll, attempting it in pitch darkness might impose a -3 dice penalty to your roll if the Storyteller wanted to acknowledge the adverse circumstances. </div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite right.<br /> <br /> 5 is a soft-cap. See page 238 for a list of tasks with a Difficulty above 5. Or page 231 (which runs to Difficulty 20). <br /> <br /> The text on page 185 establishes that Difficulty 5 is appropriate for near impossible feats. If it's technically possible but even Batman would probably fail it, then it's Difficulty 5 (even Batman can't reliably read a letter in pitch darkness by feeling the raised ink with his fingertips, but there is at least <i>something</i> to feel so a Wuxia OTT hero might perform such a feat). 5+ is for things that just can't happen without magic -- like a human lifting a rhinoceros. Or, at least, things which are significantly harder than the hardest feats which can generally be accomplished without magic (i.e. harder than reading a letter in pitch darkness by feeling the ink on the page with your fingertips, or harder than jumping hundreds of feet and landing safely, or harder than running for three days straight without sleep or rest).<br /> <br /> Further page 188 states &quot;Most of the time, advantageous or disadvantageous environmental factors will simply determine the difficulty of an action, rather than producing penalties or bonuses.&quot;<br /> <br /> Performing a &quot;simple&quot; surgery is listed on page 185 as a Difficulty 1 action for heroic characters. (I'd suggest Difficulty 2 for run-of-the-mill characters.) Performing it in pitch darkness does not impose a penalty, it just raises the Difficulty to 2 (I'd suggest 4 for non-heroic characters).<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> For run-of-the-mill, non-heroic characters (but bear in mind that anyone who is standing up to, or fighting beside, the Exalted is probably not &quot;run-of-the-mill&quot;), I'd keep trivial actions as unrolled (no rolling to the your shoes), or Difficulty 1 if failure has a meaningful consequence. Difficulty 1 actions either stay at 1 or get bumped to 2 (an average professional should succeed - a lock smith with Dex 2 Larceny 1 Specialty in Lockpicking, Craft: Locks 2, should be able to pick a lock, but some actions are going to require Willpower or exceptional tools to pull off every time). Difficulty 2 actions become 3 or 4. Difficulty 3 actions become Difficulty 5. Run-of-the-mill characters auto-fail Difficulty 4 and 5 actions -- a merely average equestrian can't break a wild, man-eating horse in the middle of a forest fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-10-2020, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T04:52:15-07:00","id":1402044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401984#post1401984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;As great heroes, Exalted characters are assumed to possess abundant confdence and competence. Tasks which run-of-the-mill individuals in Creation would consider challenging (such as picking a lock or removing a patient\u2019s appendix without killing him) are ordinary fare for heroes. Such tasks are appropriate for difficulty 1.&quot;<br /> <br /> Heroic characters use the heroic difficulty chart. Run-of-the-mill characters don't.<br /> <br /> A heroic priest can perform surgery at night in a storm 73% of the time. Your average priest cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div> But if the heroic priest gets in a medicine contest with the ordinary priest, they each have an equal chance of success because it's an opposed roll?<br /> <br /> In something more likely to occur in play, a heroic character sneaking past an ordinary character is a common situation in fiction and roleplaying. The way this is set up in the rules, if the mortal has a typical dice pool, the difficulty is comparable to some truly incredible heroic feats.<br /> <br /> Hitting battle-ready troops with a decisive attack is also equivalent to plucking a gem from a nest of writhing serpents without being bitten while the temple collapses around you.<br /> <br /> IMO having a single difficulty scale for everyone and giving heroic characters larger pools relative to non-heroic characters (or not letting non-heroic characters double 10s, or making stunt bonuses bigger) would be a more solid basis for a system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T06:19:24-07:00","id":1402055,"title":"","content":"Why would you use a decisive attack against a battle group? They don\u2019t have health levels, they have magnitude, and withering does magnitude just fine.<br /> <br /> (Pop, pop!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T06:22:40-07:00","id":1402057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402055#post1402055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you use a decisive attack against a battle group? They don\u2019t have health levels, they have magnitude, and withering does magnitude just fine.<br /> <br /> (Pop, pop!)</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's just one battle-ready troop. Like a soldier separated from their unit for whatever reason, heroic character gets in a 1 v 1 fight with them, seems like a pretty common occurrence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T06:23:18-07:00","id":1402058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402044#post1402044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But if the heroic priest gets in a medicine contest with the ordinary priest, they each have an equal chance of success because it's an opposed roll?<br /> <br /> In something more likely to occur in play, a heroic character sneaking past an ordinary character is a common situation in fiction and roleplaying. The way this is set up in the rules, if the mortal has a typical dice pool, the difficulty is comparable to some truly incredible heroic feats.<br /> <br /> Hitting battle-ready troops with a decisive attack is also equivalent to plucking a gem from a nest of writhing serpents without being bitten while the temple collapses around you.<br /> <br /> IMO having a single difficulty scale for everyone and giving heroic characters larger pools relative to non-heroic characters (or not letting non-heroic characters double 10s, or making stunt bonuses bigger) would be a more solid basis for a system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with you but I didn't develop 3E. I'm only commenting on how the game is.<br /> <br /> But to address your points:<br /> <br /> The heroic priest is going to be Stunting, for +2 dice at least. And if you are a doctor going head to head with House... that's pretty damn heroic. Dr. Chase is a heroic doctor, he just has Medicine 4 not 5.<br /> <br /> If your master Night is sneaking past an ordinary person then I probably wouldn't even make you roll.<br /> <br /> And you use &quot;troops&quot; plural. As in &quot;my singular great hero is probably fighting solo against an entire battlegroup of these troops&quot;. Yeah, sure, fighting a single battle ready troop is difficult compared to the p185 difficulties, but if you look at the Skip It sidebar on page 212 You can defeat that single battle ready soldier with a single Difficulty 2 melee roll (which is much more in line with the difficulties on p185).<br /> <br /> The system is cinematic. If you're fighting run-of-the-mill mooks, they're probably a battle group or trivial opponents. The difficulties aren't simulationist, they're dramatic according to the narrative. Check p229 -- demolishing a wall takes an hour and needs ten successes... unless it's &quot;totally f***ing bitchin'&quot; for you to burst through like the Kool Aid guy, in which case it takes 0.02 seconds and you don't have to roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T06:58:03-07:00","id":1402063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402055#post1402055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you use a decisive attack against a battle group? They don\u2019t have health levels, they have magnitude, and withering does magnitude just fine.<br /> <br /> (Pop, pop!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Decisive attacks can do more damage (depending on variables like soak and initiative).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1453-henry","name":"Henry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T08:22:23-07:00","id":1402071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402058#post1402058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't disagree with you but I didn't develop 3E. I'm only commenting on how the game is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's completely fair.<br /> <br /> My convention is that the game overall hangs together better if you pretend that section gives difficulty numbers that are a little bit higher.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The heroic priest is going to be Stunting, for +2 dice at least. And if you are a doctor going head to head with House... that's pretty damn heroic. Dr. Chase is a heroic doctor, he just has Medicine 4 not 5. </div> </div> </div>A priest who stunts can do an appendectomy at night in a storm 81% of the time. For a non-heroic priest with your suggested non-heroic difficulty, that's 33% to 13%. Here we see that the badass heroic priest can pull off the operation in extreme conditions without much difficulty, while the ordinary priest will probably fail, but might succeed with luck.<br /> <br /> On an opposed roll, the stunting heroic priest has a 59% chance of victory, if I did the math right, and the ordinary priest has a 24% chance of victory. So beating, or even tying, the non-stunting priest at a medicine challenge is significantly harder than doing the appendectomy without sufficient light in a storm. <br /> <br /> These characters aren't top expert doctors like Dr. House. They're warrior priests, which I guess makes them priests first, warriors second, doctors at best third. (Maybe they're from competing religions trying to convert the people of a small village by proving their superiority at healing the sick.)<br /> <br /> If your master Night is sneaking past an ordinary person then I probably wouldn't even make you roll.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> For analyzing this, I think it's best to consider heroic mortal characters. (One could also consider Exalts who don't have access to their Excellencies.) For Exalts with a significant Excellency, the hardest difficulties are an everyday occurrence (which, OK, that's what an Exalt is) so it's harder to say what's reasonable or not.<br /> <br /> Another scenario, which comes up a lot for me in play, is that a Night and another Solar who's not specialized in Stealth, but has a few levels, want to sneak into a place together. I don't think we were ever sneaking past a single ordinary human guard, but we experienced the general phenomenon that opposed rolls are much easier to fail then rolls vs. a static difficulty or anything that involves a series of rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you use &quot;troops&quot; plural. As in &quot;my singular great hero is probably fighting solo against an entire battlegroup of these troops&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I can think of a lot of scenes in fiction where a heroic character has to fight a single enemy soldier. For a combat-focused heroic character, this is of course going to be a cinch, but for fictional characters equivalent to a heroic mortal with some combat abilities or a Solar with almost no combat stats, this is difficult enough to be worth playing out (depending on its narrative importance...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, sure, fighting a single battle ready troop is difficult compared to the p185 difficulties, but if you look at the Skip It sidebar on page 212 You can defeat that single battle ready soldier with a single Difficulty 2 melee roll (which is much more in line with the difficulties on p185). </div> </div> </div>The fact that the Difficulty to defeat the soldier instantaneously is half the difficulty of hitting them once kind of demonstrates my point that the difficulties don't match up with the numbers on the QCs. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The system is cinematic. If you're fighting run-of-the-mill mooks, they're probably a battle group or trivial opponents. The difficulties aren't simulationist, they're dramatic according to the narrative. Check p229 -- demolishing a wall takes an hour and needs ten successes... unless it's &quot;totally f***ing bitchin'&quot; for you to burst through like the Kool Aid guy, in which case it takes 0.02 seconds and you don't have to roll. </div> </div> </div>100% agreed on this. It would be cruel of my ST to either make me roll Athletics or spend motes on Monkey Leap Technique when I describe my character doing sweet jumps in combat. But it can also be cinematic for heroic characters to fail at certain things and get into trouble.<br /> <br /> Totally unrelated to any debate, here's a &quot;fun&quot; exercise - evaluate the Difficulty of these feats from the gpt3 navy seal copypasta:<br /> <br /> 1. <span style=\"color:#141415\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">My sense of hearing is so keen that I can detect my enemy's movement by the sound of his blood pumping through his veins.<br /> 2. I can smell the sweat of my enemy as he holds his breath in my presence.<br /> 3. My physical endurance is so extreme that I can swim 100m, with full combat gear, underwater, with 60lbs of weights strapped to my ankles in 52 seconds.<br /> 4. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#141415\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I can see dust particles that are smaller than the head of a pin from a mile away.<br /> 5. My grip is so powerful I can crush boulders and destroy trees with a flick of my wrist.<br /> 6. I have been running 25 miles every day, pushing a military spec Humvee in front of me.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> I have Difficulty 4 for the first one (it seems significantly easier than reading paper by touch), Difficulty 1 for the second one, and Difficulty 6 for the fourth one (it seems significantly harder than reading paper by touch), but I'm not sure about the rest.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T09:33:21-07:00","id":1402082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402071#post1402071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A priest who stunts can do an appendectomy at night in a storm 81% of the time. For a non-heroic priest with your suggested non-heroic difficulty, that's 33% to 13%. Here we see that the badass heroic priest can pull off the operation in extreme conditions without much difficulty, while the ordinary priest will probably fail, but might succeed with luck.<br /> <br /> On an opposed roll, the stunting heroic priest has a 59% chance of victory, if I did the math right, and the ordinary priest has a 24% chance of victory. So beating, or even tying, the non-stunting priest at a medicine challenge is significantly harder than doing the appendectomy without sufficient light in a storm. <br /> <br /> These characters aren't top expert doctors like Dr. House. They're warrior priests, which I guess makes them priests first, warriors second, doctors at best third. (Maybe they're from competing religions trying to convert the people of a small village by proving their superiority at healing the sick.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Xena, warrior princess, is not an expert doctor. She's a warrior princess. But she can effortlessly straighten dislocated limbs without complications because she's a heroic character. An actual, trained doctor, in the Hercules universe doesn't have so easy a time of it.<br /> <br /> If a heroic priest is getting in a competition with an average priest, my contention is that the average priest shouldn't get to roll. If the average priest is good enough to challenge the heroic, protagonist, of the story (as Dr. Chase challenges Dr. House, despite the former being the latter's protege) then they are heroic by default.<br /> <br /> If I wanted a PC doctor to prove she was better than an NPC, I wouldn't use an opposed roll for that. I'd look at the Skip It sidebar and make it one Difficulty 2 roll for the PC. If it were a warrior priest (warrior first, priest second, doctor third) PC with 1 dot in Medicine and Intelligence 3 vs an actual, trained doctor, run-of-the-mill NPC (QC with Healing the Sick 4 dice), then I might have an opposed roll... but it's not egrigious that someone who isn't a doctor might struggle against someone who is a doctor in a competition of doctoring. And yes, beating this random NPC would be harder than doing actual doctoring, but that actual doctoring is very unlikely to be doctoring for doctoring's sake. When Xena relocates her own dislocated arm, it's not because Xena being a good doctor is important to the narrative -- it's because Xena being able to fight on despite injury is important to the narrative.<br /> <br /> Flip it on it's head and the run-of-the-mill priest has a 23% chance of performing an appendectomy at night in a storm and a 24% chance of beating a heroic priest who could reliably perform that surgery. The system works for the person rolling the dice. Why are average NPCs rolling dice?<br /> <br /> (Also, remember ties go to the better stunt.)<br /> <br /> If you try to order beer at a bar, the ST should not be calling for Bargain rolls against the Bartenders Resolve of 3. Even though you are Bargaining and Resolve sets the Difficulty of that action.<br /> <br /> The point is that the difficulties aren't fixed -- they're cinematic.<br /> <br /> &quot;Only imperial storm troopers are this accurate.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402071#post1402071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally unrelated to any debate, here's a &quot;fun&quot; exercise - evaluate the Difficulty of these feats from the gpt3 navy seal copypasta:<br /> <br /> 1. <span style=\"color:#141415\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">My sense of hearing is so keen that I can detect my enemy's movement by the sound of his blood pumping through his veins.<br /> 2. I can smell the sweat of my enemy as he holds his breath in my presence.<br /> 3. My physical endurance is so extreme that I can swim 100m, with full combat gear, underwater, with 60lbs of weights strapped to my ankles in 52 seconds.<br /> 4. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#141415\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I can see dust particles that are smaller than the head of a pin from a mile away.<br /> 5. My grip is so powerful I can crush boulders and destroy trees with a flick of my wrist.<br /> 6. I have been running 25 miles every day, pushing a military spec Humvee in front of me.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> I have Difficulty 4 for the first one (it seems significantly easier than reading paper by touch), Difficulty 1 for the second one, and Difficulty 6 for the fourth one (it seems significantly harder than reading paper by touch), but I'm not sure about the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. 5 -- certainly pumping blood is more obvious than a thin layer of ink, but distance is also a factor as is movement. 4 to hear someone's heartbeat, 5 to track them by heartbeat.<br /> 2. 2. Finding your enemy is Difficulty 1, the added complication of doing it by smell raises it to 2.<br /> 3. 5. Kyle Chamers took freestyle 100m gold with 47.58s. 52 seconds, fully dressed and weighed down is essentially impossible.<br /> 4. 8. Comparable to &quot;riddles which unlock or reveal <br /> the greatest secrets of Creation\u2019s history&quot; or lifting a rhinoceros. This is significantly off the scale.<br /> 5. 18. This is actually on the Feats of Strength chart.<br /> 6. 5. This one is actually possible. I was there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-10-2020, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T09:50:28-07:00","id":1402085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402082#post1402082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. 18. This is actually on the Feats of Strength chart.<br /> 6. 5. This one is actually possible. I was there.</div> </div> </div> </div>#5 also would require strength 10 to even attempt - for a non-magical human it's impossible.<br /> I'd be inclined to mark several others of these as impossible for a non-magical human, #3 and 4 in particular.<br /> <br /> #6 Sounds similar to one of the strength 5, difficulty 5 feats of strength in the book, with the added specification that it takes place over 25 miles, requires running speed instead of whatever speed is assumed for that feat of strength, and happens every day. I'm not sure how those affect the difficulty - they partially sound more like separate rolls than single high difficulty roll - one to move the humvee, and one to keep going for 25 miles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T10:01:43-07:00","id":1402087,"title":"","content":"I also don't take the extra successes to be too meaningful from the perspective of in-setting effects. Getting 30 successes rather than 5 on a craft: cooking result doesn't make food that rewires the brains of those who eat it with pure delight any more than getting 30 successes on a tie shoes roll lets the characters jump all of the way to yu-shan. Close to perfect is close to perfect and the amount of variance that's available as one asymptotically approaches true perfection doesn't translate into game mechanical effects.<br /> <br /> I also think that adding more bookkeeping for bonus successes in craft is not a change that I can get behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T10:28:16-07:00","id":1402090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402085#post1402085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#5 also would require strength 10 to even attempt - for a non-magical human it's impossible.<br /> I'd be inclined to mark several others of these as impossible for a non-magical human, #3 and 4 in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for fun. Waiving the strength requirement, without magic.<br /> <br /> Strength 5. Athletics 5. Specialty in Badassery. 3 point stunt.<br /> <br /> 99.97% of the time you look a fool.<br /> <br /> But 0.03% of the time, you are Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T11:14:57-07:00","id":1402092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402090#post1402090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for fun. Waiving the strength requirement, without magic.<br /> <br /> Strength 5. Athletics 5. Specialty in Badassery. 3 point stunt.<br /> <br /> 99.97% of the time you look a fool.<br /> <br /> But 0.03% of the time, you are Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>With mighty thews 3 and a willpower, you hit 18 successes 1.13% of the time.<br /> <br /> Also, I love the specialty in Badassery, though it might be a bit overpowered for an Exalted character. Under what circumstances does it not apply?<br /> <br /> With magic<br /> A solar or lunar with a full 10-die excellency makes it 32% of the time.<br /> An essence 1 sidereal with a full excellency makes it 51% of the time, at essence 5 it goes to 89%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T12:41:38-07:00","id":1402104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402011#post1402011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Essence is gonna shake the difficulty chart out slightly.<br /> <br /> Like... &quot;Difficulties for things that Exalts should bother rolling for should START at 3. Beating up a group of drunks when you're a goddamn Exalt would be Difficulty 3 and easier tasks, don't bother rolling&quot; and I think I recall hearing the game may have charts for what 7 successes or more would mean for Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I can see the wisdom of Exalted Essence starting from difficulty 3. <br /> <br /> Traditionally it has makes sense to start from 1. Since with 9 attributes and 25 abilities, its not inconceivable to find yourself in a situation where performing a basic task is pretty difficult. However, with attributes and abilities being streamlined there is going to be an inevitable increase in baseline competence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T18:31:52-07:00","id":1402157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402092#post1402092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I love the specialty in Badassery, though it might be a bit overpowered for an Exalted character. Under what circumstances does it not apply?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my players basically has a specialty in Stunts. Before he Exalted he was a street performer for cash to pay his tuition giving, him a Melee specialty in Sword Tricks. So whenever he does a melee stunt its usually a cool circus trick.<br /> <br /> It's really cool and fits his character well, and he's not a powergamer so there you go. A specialty in Badassery. <br /> <br /> Showing Off is another good one I've seen. Usually it helps offset the higher DC of cool shit. Of course, the best specialty is XYZ (While Naked)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T03:39:49-07:00","id":1403204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1402011#post1402011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Essence is gonna shake the difficulty chart out slightly.<br /> <br /> Like... &quot;Difficulties for things that Exalts should bother rolling for should START at 3. Beating up a group of drunks when you're a goddamn Exalt would be Difficulty 3 and easier tasks, don't bother rolling&quot; and I think I recall hearing the game may have charts for what 7 successes or more would mean for Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just makes me think of the &quot;these go up to 11&quot; skit, i.e. would it not be more practical to just bring what all of the numbers signify down a few notches rather than render the first few dots in a stat kind of worthless?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T05:54:56-07:00","id":1403212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401821-random-thought-on-threshold-successes?p=1401984#post1401984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroic characters use the heroic difficulty chart. Run-of-the-mill characters don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, now <i>this</i> is something... I\u2019m <i>not</i> going to do. Exalted is a much better game for the fact that \u201cCombat Movement: 4 dice\u201d means that entire Realm legion can do parkour in heavy rain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}